---
import PreviewLayout from '../../layouts/PreviewLayout.astro';
import RelatedPosts from '../../components/RelatedPosts.astro';

const title = "Uncle Robert's Wednesday Night Market: The Real Puna Experience | Island Goodes";
const relatedPosts = [
  { slug: "hilo-farmers-market", title: "Hilo Farmers Market Guide", image: "/images/blog/farmers-market.webp", category: "Food" },
  { slug: "downtown-hilo-guide", title: "A Local's Guide to Downtown Hilo", image: "/images/blog/downtown-hilo.webp", category: "Guide" },
  { slug: "best-poke-hilo", title: "Best Poke in Hilo", image: "/images/blog/poke-bowl.webp", category: "Food" }
];
const description = "Experience authentic Hawaiian culture at Uncle Robert's Wednesday Night Market in Kalapana. Live music, awa bar, local food, and the spirit of Puna.";
const publishDate = "2025-11-20";
---

<PreviewLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="blog-post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <div class="post-header-bg">
        <img src="/images/blog/uncle-roberts.webp" alt="Local food at Uncle Robert's Night Market" />
      </div>
      <div class="post-header-overlay"></div>
      <div class="post-header-content">
        <nav class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blog">Blog</a> / Uncle Robert's Night Market
        </nav>
        <span class="post-category">Events & Culture</span>
        <h1>Uncle Robert's Wednesday Night Market</h1>
        <p class="post-tagline">The Real Puna Experience</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <time datetime={publishDate}>November 20, 2025</time>
          <span class="read-time">5 min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="lead">
          If you want to experience authentic Hawaiian culture—not the tourist version—there's
          no better place than Uncle Robert's Wednesday Night Market in Kalapana. It's a weekly
          celebration of Puna spirit: live music, traditional awa (kava), local food, and a
          community that welcomes visitors with genuine aloha.
        </p>

        <div class="info-box">
          <h3>Quick Facts</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>When:</strong> Every Wednesday, 4pm-10pm</li>
            <li><strong>Where:</strong> Kalapana, Puna District</li>
            <li><strong>From Island Goodes:</strong> 45 minutes via Highway 130</li>
            <li><strong>Admission:</strong> $10 (cash only)</li>
            <li><strong>Parking:</strong> Free, arrive early for best spots</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>What to Expect</h2>
        <p>
          Uncle Robert's isn't just a market—it's a party. The centerpiece is the awa bar,
          where you can try the traditional Polynesian drink made from kava root. It's relaxing,
          earthy, and completely legal. Sitting at the awa bar, you'll meet locals, hear stories,
          and feel the genuine warmth of Hawaiian hospitality.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Kalapana Awa Band provides live music every week, playing Hawaiian and reggae-influenced
          tunes that keep the atmosphere mellow and happy. Bring a blanket or low chair to sit on
          the grass and soak it all in.
        </p>

        <h2>The Food</h2>
        <p>
          Multiple food vendors offer everything from Hawaiian plate lunches to Thai food, tacos,
          fresh fruit smoothies, and desserts. Quality is consistently good—these are local
          cooks who take pride in their food. Cash only at most vendors.
        </p>

        <div class="highlight-box">
          <h4>Must-Try at Uncle Robert's:</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Shell of awa (kava) at the bar—start with one!</li>
            <li>Fresh coconut water from whole coconuts</li>
            <li>Kalua pork plate lunch</li>
            <li>Lilikoi (passionfruit) anything</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>The Craft Fair</h2>
        <p>
          Local artisans sell handmade goods: jewelry made from local materials, tie-dye clothing,
          woodwork, art, and Hawaiian crafts. Prices are reasonable, and you're buying directly
          from the makers. It's the opposite of tourist-trap shopping.
        </p>

        <h2>Tips for Your Visit</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><strong>Bring cash</strong> - Most vendors and the awa bar are cash-only</li>
          <li><strong>Arrive by 5pm</strong> - Best parking and less crowded early on</li>
          <li><strong>Bring a blanket or low chair</strong> - Seating is on the grass</li>
          <li><strong>Wear comfortable clothes</strong> - It's casual and laid-back</li>
          <li><strong>Don't drive if you drink awa</strong> - It can affect coordination</li>
          <li><strong>Respect the space</strong> - This is a community gathering, not just a tourist attraction</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The Drive to Kalapana</h2>
        <p>
          The drive from Island Goodes takes about 45 minutes via Highway 130 through the Puna
          district. It's a scenic route through papaya farms and tropical forest. The road is
          well-maintained but winding in places—take your time.
        </p>

        <p>
          You'll pass through Pahoa, a funky little town worth exploring if you have time before
          the market. The area around Kalapana was covered by lava flows from Kilauea in 1990,
          and again in 2018—you'll see the stark lava fields as you approach.
        </p>

        <h2>Saturday Market Alternative</h2>
        <p>
          If Wednesday doesn't work for your schedule, Uncle Robert's also hosts a Saturday
          morning market (8am-noon). It's smaller and more low-key—fresh produce, local food,
          crafts—but lacks the live music and awa bar atmosphere of Wednesday night.
        </p>

        <div class="cta-box">
          <h3>Experience Puna from Island Goodes</h3>
          <p>
            Stay with us and explore the authentic side of the Big Island. Uncle Robert's is
            just one of many unique experiences within easy reach of your room.
          </p>
          <a href="/book" class="btn btn-primary">Book Your Stay</a>
        </div>

        <RelatedPosts posts={relatedPosts} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</PreviewLayout>

<style>
  .post-header { position: relative; min-height: 50vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; color: #fff; padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem; }
  .post-header-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -2; }
  .post-header-bg img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .post-header-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1; background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,0.3) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.7) 100%); }
  .post-header-content { max-width: 800px; }
  .post-category { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-secondary); color: #1a1a1a; padding: 0.375rem 1rem; border-radius: 50px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .post-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .post-tagline { font-size: 1.25rem; opacity: 0.9; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .post-meta { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; justify-content: center; opacity: 0.9; font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  .post-content { padding: var(--section-padding) 0; }
  .container.narrow { max-width: 750px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  .post-content h2 { color: var(--color-text); font-size: 1.75rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .post-content p { color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

  .info-box { background: var(--gradient-primary); padding: 2rem; border-radius: 16px; color: #fff; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .info-box h3 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .info-box ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; }
  .info-box li { padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); }
  .info-box li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .info-box strong { color: var(--color-secondary-light); }

  .highlight-box { background: var(--color-bg-alt); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .highlight-box h4 { color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .highlight-box ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; }
  .highlight-box li { padding: 0.375rem 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; position: relative; color: var(--color-text-light); }
  .highlight-box li::before { content: "•"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-secondary); }

  .checklist { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .checklist li { padding: 0.75rem 0; padding-left: 1.75rem; position: relative; color: var(--color-text-light); border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; }
  .checklist li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .checklist li::before { content: "✓"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 600; }
  .checklist strong { color: var(--color-text); }

  .cta-box { background: var(--gradient-primary); padding: 2.5rem; border-radius: 16px; text-align: center; color: #fff; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .cta-box h3 { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .cta-box p { opacity: 0.9; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
</style>
